{"title":"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906fddead65545297c74bbc2ca83cd01f3f9ecc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> be the set of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real numbers</a>.  Determine all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/6/e769732c09eafd5777222570e5c3aba3973c47f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f : \\mathbb{R} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> such that\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfb21cc82bd37243d911f9065df15643ac93f110.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x^2 - y^2) = xf(x) - yf(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"217\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>for all pairs of real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We first prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Odd_function\" title=\"Odd function\"> odd</a>.\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/547a5b8076d52eeb9c73444e3334ef47a6865980.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0) = f(x^2 - x^2) = xf(x) - xf(x) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"312\" height=\"19\" />, and for nonzero <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/e/a9e699be480c2800d98144fde50bf1796b99f1cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xf(x) + yf(-y) = f(x^2 - y^2) = xf(x) - yf(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"371\" height=\"21\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/4/a74fa37e179315d78a70b88a654c3d7956ae9519.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$yf(-y) = -yf(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"20\" />, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/e/24e1f9cb12176857c846c9bcb98da29f35d61468.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(-y) = -f(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />.  Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is odd.  Henceforth, we shall assume that all variables are non-negative.\n</p><p>If we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a06334068417b1781d14e8b28af827907961eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, then we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/23082831f4c78251aa9f7e951113f29cb934827e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x^2) = xf(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"19\" />.  Therefore the problem's condition becomes\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84eb65e6105575ab580a1f4b54b729563419e830.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x^2 - y^2) + f(y^2) = f(x^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"215\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>But for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />, we may set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7dbac5105c1f55e9ecb7d9184f7365882effa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\sqrt{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/f/fcfc3e170e93d8d56e51cec015e9bf1e847c7307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\sqrt{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"21\" /> to obtain\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ece4bb7e38fbaa6a39eabe6dd198a498db7c2ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a-b) + f(b) = f(a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>(It is well known that the only <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Continuous\" title=\"Continuous\">continuous</a> solutions to this functional equation are of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52c93d9c36f90fa078b1a5448a1c2982b4588da0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = kx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, but there do exist other solutions to this which are not solutions to the equation of this problem.)\n</p><p>We may let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/b/74b1aa3440c020dc20fdb065411df1cedd700d00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2t$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/c/a4c890f51f6fe94b673f06a43555e8057e817659.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/4/d54d77b49c9a05e41c146acd62d575ed1d2abce6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2f(t) = f(2t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/8/5886e054ae3c5f9031594fc2e17990ee17885a06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = t+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/442763f02c8abe0ff2542f403d3d03453f1d2420.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> in the original condition yields\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/763f52af0b477acc7565d7ef9e88ab401dd5c166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{matrix}f(2t+1) &amp;=&amp; (t+1)f(t+1) - tf(t) \\qquad \\\\ &amp;=&amp; (t+1)[f(t) + f(1) ] - tf(t) \\\\ &amp;=&amp; f(t) + (t+1)f(1) \\qquad \\qquad \\end{matrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -24px\" width=\"328\" height=\"58\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>But we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7add4e77bf5f62f8c1af87371728bdaceacd8ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2t + 1) = f(2t) + f(1) = 2f(t) + f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"312\" height=\"18\" />, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/3/df3a1cfaac47685692d8a4bd135e07812cc2bf17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2f(t) + f(1) = f(t) + tf(1) + f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"270\" height=\"18\" />, or\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/179669ecacf26e786e216e97d828cc20ab225edb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(t) = tf(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Hence all solutions to our equation are of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52c93d9c36f90fa078b1a5448a1c2982b4588da0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = kx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />.  It is easy to see that real value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> will suffice.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>As in the first solution, we obtain the result that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> satisfies the condition\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/5/f859f05debb01c6e5218c22cf6a7715e7a450bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a) + f(b) = f(a+b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>We note that\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/3/a73908d89b8fa5f4e3ddba2d3bdad333c4b03c16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = f\\left[ \\left(\\frac{x+1}{2}\\right)^2 - \\left( \\frac{x-1}{2} \\right)^2 \\right] = \\frac{x+1}{2} f \\left( \\frac{x+1}{2} \\right) - \\frac{x-1}{2} f \\left( \\frac{x-1}{2} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"586\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4df183927fe48ac0e49b6010eca74aba5645782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2t) = 2f(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" />, this is equal to\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7e25a777a70a3ceeb70aec2022dcc9b770c64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(x+1)[f(x) +f(1)]}{4} - \\frac{(x-1)[f(x) - f(1)]}{4} = \\frac{xf(1) + f(x)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"474\" height=\"39\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> must be of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52c93d9c36f90fa078b1a5448a1c2982b4588da0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = kx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO\" title=\"2002 USAMO\">2002 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2002\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017201216\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 249/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1663/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7318/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.614      1 -total\n 37.15%    6.544      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 31.24%    5.502      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 30.10%    5.301      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4637:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017201216 and revision id 282156. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}